==============================================================================
READING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Link 1 is a clean THEOREM: any gcd-1 set whose residues mod (2n-1) avoid 0
 and miss an antipodal pair clears the gap (M>=2/(2n-1)), witnessed by t_k,
 k=a^{-1}. This collapses the ENTIRE gap conjecture onto the 2^(n-1) perfect
 transversals of the antipodal pairs -- the AP being the all-lower transversal.
 The reduced conjecture: among transversal-configs only the AP-tight family
 reaches below 2/(2n-1). Each one-flip neighbor of the AP is the next chain link.
